--- !u!114 &1665512598
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1665512595}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 79264283c8b494d419a1147d41b751b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteSheet
  title: OBSERVATION, LAMBERT B.
  content: '<b>Day 1</b>, Nurse M.

    Calm, polite, cooperative. Reports hearing a voice that repeats "thirteen." No other disturbance noted.


    <b>Day 3</b>, Nurse M.

    Says the voice is gone and that he feels fine. <i>Denial of illness.</i>


    <b>Day 8</b>, Dr. R.

    Waits outside the dining hall an hour before mealtime. <i>Oral fixation.</i>

    Keeps telling the other patients he is not ill. One of them replies: "I know."


    <b>Day 13</b>, Nurse L.

    Counts the hallway tiles out loud. Claims that his bedroom door "doesn''t always open onto the hallway." <i>Delusion becoming systematized.</i>


    <b>Day 24</b>, Dr. R.

    Now answers only with numbers. Says he is "looking for the right number." Says people no longer see him. Talks to his door.

    <i>Depersonalization. Dosage increased.</i>


    <b>Day 41</b>, Nurse M.

    No longer eats. No longer sleeps. Writes "13" on the wall every day. Cleaned off, started again.

    <i>(Handwritten note in the margin: "What if he was right?")</i>


    <b>Day 52, November 13</b>, Dr. R.

    Patient did not answer roll call. Room 13: bed unmade, door closed from the inside.

    File closed: <b>schizophrenia in remission.</b>'
  reaction:
    text: "<i>They blamed everything on the illness. What if that wasn\u2019t it?</i>"
    clip: {fileID: 0}
  reactionPlayed: 0
